.TH DARPA-SPILLSERVER-BOOTSTRAP 1 "September 24, 2026" "darpa_spillserver 1.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
darpa-spillserver-bootstrap \- set up a DARPA-SpillServer checkout: venv, packages and C/C++ library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.RB [ PYTHON=\fIexe\fR ]
.RB [ EXTRAS=\fIlist\fR ]
.RB [ BUILD_CPP=auto | yes | no ]
.RB [ NOVA_TIME_DECODER_DIR=\fIdir\fR ]
.B ./bootstrap.sh
.PP
.B .\e bootstrap.ps1
.RB [ \-Python
.IR exe ]
.RB [ \-Extras
.IR list ]
.RB [ \-BuildCpp
.BR auto | yes | no ]
.RB [ \-DecoderDir
.IR dir ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prepares a checkout to run.
.B bootstrap.sh
is for Linux and macOS;
.B bootstrap.ps1
for Windows 11. Both are safe to re-run: they update an existing virtual
environment and build tree in place.
.IP 1. 4
Find a Python 3.9 or newer. The NOvA gateway nodes ship Python 3.6, so the
shell script also looks for a private interpreter under
.I ~/.local/opt/python3.1[1\-3]
before trying
.BR python3.13 " \(en " python3.9 ,
.B python3
and
.BR python ;
if none qualifies it prints how to install one without root. The PowerShell
script tries the
.B py \-3
launcher, then
.BR python .
.IP 2. 4
Create or reuse
.IR venv/ ,
and upgrade pip.
.IP 3. 4
Install
.B nova\-time\-decoder
in editable mode from a checkout, if one is found at
.BR NOVA_TIME_DECODER_DIR / \-DecoderDir ,
.IR ../nova\-time\-decoder ,
or
.IR ../../nova\-time\-decoder ,
so a fix there is picked up without reinstalling. Otherwise it comes from the
package index.
.IP 4. 4
Install
.I requirements.txt
(without its
.B nova\-time\-decoder
line when a checkout was used), then the package itself in editable mode with
the chosen extras.
.IP 5. 4
If CMake is available, configure, build and test the C/C++ client library in
.IR build/ :
.B cmake \-\-preset default
on Linux and macOS,
.B cmake \-\-preset windows\-msvc
on Windows (which needs vcpkg at
.BR $VCPKG_ROOT ),
then
.BR "cmake \-\-build" " and " ctest .
With
.B auto
a failed or impossible build is reported and set-up continues; with
.B yes
it is an error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR PYTHON ", " \-Python " " \fIexe\fR
Interpreter to use; it must be 3.9 or newer.
.TP
.BR EXTRAS ", " \-Extras " " \fIlist\fR
pip extras installed with the package. Default \fBtest\fR; \fBdev\fR adds the
OIDC dependencies, \fBoidc\fR installs only those.
.TP
.BR BUILD_CPP ", " \-BuildCpp " " \fBauto\fR|\fByes\fR|\fBno\fR
Whether to build the C/C++ library. Default \fBauto\fR: build when
.B cmake
is on
.BR PATH .
.TP
.BR NOVA_TIME_DECODER_DIR ", " \-DecoderDir " " \fIdir\fR
A
.B nova\-time\-decoder
checkout to install from.
.PP
The PowerShell parameters default to the same environment variables.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I venv/
The virtual environment.
.TP
.I requirements.txt
.TQ
.I requirements\-dev.txt
Runtime, and test and optional, Python dependencies.
.TP
.I build/
CMake build tree, including
.B darpa\-spill\-client\-cpp
and
.BR libdarpa_spill_client .
.TP
.I docs/GETTING_STARTED.md
.TQ
.I docs/CPP_LIBRARY.md
Installing prerequisites on each platform.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Set-up finished. The last line reports what happened to the C/C++ build.
.TP
.B non-zero
No suitable Python, a pip failure, or (with
.BR BUILD_CPP=yes )
a C/C++ build failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.EX
\&./bootstrap.sh
PYTHON=python3.12 BUILD_CPP=no ./bootstrap.sh
EXTRAS=dev NOVA_TIME_DECODER_DIR=~/src/nova\-time\-decoder ./bootstrap.sh
.EE
.RE
.PP
On Windows:
.PP
.RS
.EX
powershell \-ExecutionPolicy Bypass \-File .\e bootstrap.ps1
\&.\e bootstrap.ps1 \-Python C:\e Python312\e python.exe \-BuildCpp no
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start-darpa-spillserver (1),
.BR stop-darpa-spillserver (1),
.BR darpa-spill-server (1),
.BR darpa-spill-client-cpp (1)
.SH REPORTING BUGS
Report defects at
\fBhttps://github.com/NovaDAQ/DARPA\-SpillServer/issues\fR.
.SH AUTHOR
NOvA DAQ group, Fermi National Accelerator Laboratory.
